From: Sergio Marin <sergio.marin@pantacor.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rdawlan: restore AP mode so the provisioning AP works

The forward-port built this driver station-only: it commented .start_ap,
.stop_ap, .change_beacon and .del_station out of the cfg80211 ops table and
correspondingly dropped NL80211_IFTYPE_AP from wiphy->interface_modes. The
functions themselves were never removed, and neither were the helpers they
call (wland_start_ap_set, wland_find_wpaie, wland_parse_tlvs,
wland_vif_set_mgmt_ie).

That breaks first-boot provisioning. pvwificonnect raises a captive-portal AP
when the device has no stored credentials, ConnMan asks cfg80211 to start one,
and there is no .start_ap to call -- so a board with no network and no serial
console cannot be provisioned at all.

Restore both halves. Registering the ops alone is not enough: without the
interface_modes bit, cfg80211 refuses an AP request before it ever reaches the
driver.

Two signatures had drifted since 3.10:

  - stop_ap gained an unsigned int link_id parameter with multi-link support.
  - del_station now takes struct station_del_parameters instead of a bare
    u8 *mac; taking the address from params->mac leaves the existing body,
    including its NULL check, unchanged.

start_ap and change_beacon needed no changes -- 6.6 still passes
cfg80211_ap_settings and cfg80211_beacon_data respectively.

mgmt_tx remains unported. It is needed for 802.11w MFP SA Query, 802.11r FT
and WNM, none of which a WPA2-PSK provisioning AP on a full-MAC part requires.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor driver, not upstream]
Signed-off-by: Sergio Marin <sergio.marin@pantacor.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/rdaw80211/rdawlan/wland_cfg80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/rdaw80211/rdawlan/wland_cfg80211.c
@@ -4559,7 +4559,8 @@ exit:
 	return err;
 }
 
-static int wland_cfg80211_stop_ap(struct wiphy *wiphy, struct net_device *ndev)
+static int wland_cfg80211_stop_ap(struct wiphy *wiphy, struct net_device *ndev,
+	unsigned int link_id)
 {
 	struct wland_if *ifp = netdev_priv(ndev);
 	s32 err = 0;
@@ -4633,8 +4634,9 @@ static s32 wland_cfg80211_change_beacon(struct wiphy *wiphy, struct net_device *
 
 #if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(3, 2, 0)
 static int wland_cfg80211_del_station(struct wiphy *wiphy, struct net_device *ndev,
-	u8 * mac)
+	struct station_del_parameters *params)
 {
+	const u8 *mac = params->mac;
 #ifdef WLAND_P2P_SUPPORT
 	struct wland_cfg80211_info *cfg = wiphy_to_cfg(wiphy);
 #endif /* WLAND_P2P_SUPPORT */
@@ -5108,12 +5110,12 @@ static struct cfg80211_ops wl_cfg80211_ops = {
 	.add_beacon = wland_cfg80211_modify_beacon,
 	.del_beacon = wland_cfg80211_modify_beacon,
 #else /* LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(3, 4, 0) */
-	/* .start_ap: dropped with .stop_ap, STA-only build */
-	/* .stop_ap: AP path, not ported for the STA-only build */
-	/* .change_beacon: AP path, not ported for the STA-only build */
+	.start_ap = wland_cfg80211_start_ap,
+	.stop_ap = wland_cfg80211_stop_ap,
+	.change_beacon = wland_cfg80211_change_beacon,
 #endif /* LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(3, 4, 0) */
 #if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(3, 2, 0)
-	/* .del_station: AP/mgmt path, not ported for the STA-only build */
+	.del_station = wland_cfg80211_del_station,
 	/* .mgmt_tx_cancel_wait: AP/mgmt path, not ported for the STA-only build */
 #endif /* LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(3, 2, 0) */
 	/* .sched_scan_start: paired with sched_scan_stop, unused */
@@ -5375,11 +5377,12 @@ static struct wiphy *wland_setup_wiphy(struct device *phydev)
 		| BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_MONITOR)
 #endif /* WLAND_MONITOR_SUPPORT */
 		/*
-		 * AP mode is not advertised: the STA-only build does not
-		 * register .start_ap/.stop_ap/.change_beacon, so claiming
-		 * the mode would let userspace ask for something we cannot
-		 * do.
+		 * AP mode: the ops are registered above, so advertise it.
+		 * Without this bit cfg80211 refuses an AP request before it
+		 * ever reaches the driver, and pvwificonnect's provisioning
+		 * AP cannot start.
 		 */
+		| BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_AP)
 #ifdef WLAND_TBD_SUPPORT
 		| BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_ADHOC)
 #endif /* WLAND_TBD_SUPPORT */
